Description: Chromium Browser Visit Sources, for visits the browser didn't make itself
Author: Glessner
Email: none
Id: 1877b601-e124-43d7-8b0a-830b4a3bb186
Version: 1.0
CSVPrefix: ChromiumBrowser
FileName: History
IdentifyQuery: SELECT count(*) FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table' AND (name='urls' OR name='visits' OR name='downloads' OR name='segments' OR name='keyword_search_terms' OR name='visit_source');
IdentifyValue: 6
Queries:
    -
        Name: Chromium Browser Visit Sources
        Query: |
                SELECT
                visit_source.id AS VisitID,
                visit_source.source AS Source
                FROM
                visit_source
                ORDER BY
                visit_source.id ASC
        BaseFileName: VisitSources

# Glessner's map, from sqlecmd_maps in its registry folder. A run of SQLECmd reads the maps in SQLECmd's own Maps
# folder and these, from a maps folder the run composes in its output folder.
#
# The visit_source table holds a row for each visit the browser didn't make itself, with the visit's ID in the visits
# table and where it came from: 0 synced from another device, 2 added by an extension, 3 imported from Firefox,
# 4 imported from Internet Explorer, and 5 imported from Safari. A visit the user browsed has no row. Glessner joins
# each row to the visit that Windows_ChromiumBrowser_HistoryVisits.smap, one of SQLECmd's maps
# (https://github.com/EricZimmerman/SQLECmd/tree/master/SQLMap/Maps), reads from the same History, by its VisitID.
# Its IdentifyQuery follows that map's, with the visit_source table added, under the license at the top.
